2026-09-16T19:41:00.8477452Z Why
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8477857Z 
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8478614Z   → Rust manifests become independently schedulable jobs per crate; Cargo resolves prerequisites inside each job while ci-required aggregates every selected result.
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8480089Z   → package.json scripts and lockfiles select the native package manager, install mode, cache, and package job.
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8481305Z   → Only checked-in, statically detected evidence controls generated commands; project code and task runners are never executed.
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8482536Z   → Generated jobs invoke `velnor-workflow run` directly; the checked-in TOML remains the runtime contract for planning, execution, policy, and release commands.
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8483272Z 
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8483434Z Boundaries
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8483625Z 
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8483973Z   ! Manifests nested under tests/ or benches/ directories are treated as test fixtures and ignored.
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8484840Z   ! No test script is declared in package.json; no package test command was invented.
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8485578Z   ! Project code, build scripts, task runners, and commands are never executed during analysis.
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8486537Z   ! Release, signing, registry, deployment, branch-protection, and runner-capability contracts remain explicit manual inputs.
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8487493Z   ! Renovate credentials, runner placement, and write permissions cannot be inferred from repository files.
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8488511Z   ! Rust build scripts are watched but their system dependencies and generated outputs are not inferred.
2026-09-16T19:41:00.8488988Z 
